===== BUG-009 structural audit (single-tree, audited RTL only) =====

----- 1. the rule the tree states for itself -----
  PASS: csrng.rdl describes INT_STATE_READ_ENABLE as a PER-INSTANCE enable
  PASS: the rdl binds each bit to the internal state of the CORRESPONDING instance
  PASS: csrng.hjson states the bit of the SELECTED instance is what must be set
  PASS: the field is a three-bit vector, one bit per instance, not a single global enable

----- 2. the port the module declares -----
  PASS: csrng_state_db declares the authorization input one bit per application
  PASS: NApps is the application count, so the vector is indexed by application
  PASS: the select, dump-select and qualified vectors are all one bit per application

----- 3. how the vector is actually consumed -----
  PASS: line 115 replicates bit 0 of the authorization vector across all NApps lanes
  PASS: line 115 carries no per-application index at all
  PASS: a per-application generate loop providing the index rd begins on the NEXT line
  PASS: int_state_read_enable_i is referenced exactly twice: its declaration and line 115
  PASS: the authorization vector is never indexed by the application being read

----- 4. the sibling lane in the same loop indexes correctly -----
  PASS: the dump SELECT in the same loop is indexed per application, so rd is in scope there
  PASS: the hardware read select is likewise per application, establishing the intended idiom
  PASS: the qualified vector is consumed per application, so lane rd carries application rd's state

----- 5. the qualified value reaches software -----
  PASS: the dumped state becomes internal_state_diag
  PASS: internal_state_diag is windowed into the 32-bit register read output
  PASS: the same internal-state layout carries the DRBG key and V, so the window exposes key material
  PASS: the reseed counter is separately and unconditionally exported, so it is NOT the sensitive part of the window

----- 6. software reachability of the authorization vector -----
  PASS: the vector is driven straight from a software-writable register field
  PASS: csrng_core wires that register field into the state database
  PASS: the field is written from the register bus, so the mask is under software control

----- evidence excerpts -----

